  "observations": [
    "The selected front physical box has a pale outer edge and dark inner edge; its face remains flat-shaded without triangle diagonals. Desktop screenshots show the corresponding stable UUID pressed in the list/inspector.",
    "Exact coincident and occluded selections retain ordinary depth behavior; a covering last-drawn box does not reveal the selected hidden box. Actual GPU patch equality separately verifies this beyond screenshot inspection.",
    "Chinese/English/Japanese 390px views show translated selection feedback guidance, retained Copper filter and selected outline outside results, with reachable sticky controls and no horizontal overflow. Some list/inspector content is below the fold and remains scrollable.",
    "The near-clipped fixture shows the real double-sided box back/sides. The gray central back surface is existing geometry, not a fabricated clipping cap. Its same-model center patch stays exactly unchanged when selecting it. Subpixel-object visibility is deliberately not promised.",
    "Legacy picking, 128-object navigation and read-only preview screenshot sets retain stable selected UUIDs, accurate Reset status, source diagnostics and truthful WebGL2-unavailable fallback.",
    "All 23 listed PNG visible regions were personally viewed. GPU per-pixel samples, whole-source/disk bytes, same-selection Reset equality and native UTF-16 location are separate browser assertions, not claims that every source byte or hidden surface was visible."
  ],
  "phaseNote": "The original failed near-clipping fixture report and producer snapshots remain intact. These screenshots all come from successful runs bound to the confirmed source manifest; no earlier or independent reviewer report has been overwritten."
